leapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2Fw0CnpPY8coVTLr2PLyev9IA_qfvg793cnKyjr9usJTw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2Fw0CnpPY8coVTLr2PLyev9IA_qfvg793cnKyjr9usJTw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>\n$(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}})_{0}=(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}})_{\\text {wire } \\mathrm{AB}}+(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}})_{\\mathrm{BC} \\mathrm{Arc}}\\quad+\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}_{\\mathrm{CD} \\text { wire }}+(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}})_{\\mathrm{PQ} \\text { wire }}\\quad+\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}_{\\mathrm{QR}(\\text { Arc })}+\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}_{\\mathrm{RS} \\text { wire }}\\quad \\mathrm{B}_{\\mathrm{PQ}}=\\mathrm{B}_{\\mathrm{RS}}=0\\quad \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}_{\\mathrm{BC}}=-\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}_{\\mathrm{QR}}(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}})_{\\mathrm{wire} \\mathrm{AB}}=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}_{\\mathrm{CD}}\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}_{\\text {net }}=(\\mathrm{B})_{\\text {wire } \\mathrm{AB}}+(\\mathrm{B})_{\\text {wire } \\mathrm{CD}}\\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mu_{0} \\mathrm{I}}{4 \\pi \\mathrm{r}}+\\frac{\\mu_{0} \\mathrm{I}}{4 \\pi \\mathrm{r}}\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}_{\\text {net }}=\\frac{\\mu_{0} \\mathrm{I}}{2 \\pi \\mathrm{r}}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2016 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d213493792ae8f35b725"},{"id":52243,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Magnetic Effects of Current","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"A beam of neutrons performs circular motion of radius, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></math> under the influence of an inhomogeneous magnetic field with inhomogeneity extending over <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Δ</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo> </mo><mi>m</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The speed of the neutrons is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>54</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> The mass and magnetic moment of the neutrons respectively are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The average variation of the magnetic field over <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Δ</mi><mi>r</mi></math> is approximately.","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>T</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo> </mo><mi>T</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo> </mo><mi>T</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo> </mo><mi>T</mi></math>"],"answer":2,"solution":"<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">ΔB=</mtext><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">v</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>Δ</mi><mi>r</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>54</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>×</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn><mo> </mo><mi>T</mi></math></p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2020 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da75ed209bf9290aded7f"},{"id":52244,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Magnetic Effects of Current","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"An electron enters a chamber in which a uniform magnetic field is present as shown. Ignore gravity.\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252FqpYkwJYlW3JoLRv3KjYA1E8o8ITw7eoUwF2hag5C9Fk.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FqpYkwJYlW3JoLRv3KjYA1E8o8ITw7eoUwF2hag5C9Fk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FqpYkwJYlW3JoLRv3KjYA1E8o8ITw7eoUwF2hag5C9Fk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>\nDuring its motion inside the chamber","options":["the force on the electron remains constant","the kinetic energy of the electron remains constant","the momentum of the electron remains constant","the speed of the electron increases at a uniform rate"],"answer":1,"solution":"$\\because$ work done $=0$\nHence kinetic energy $=$ constant","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2013 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d213cc6b7211937e6031"},{"id":52245,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Magnetic Effects of Current","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"A loop carrying current $